{"event_id":"EVT-000079","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-28T15:20:58.702Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260828T135316382114Z","run_id":"RUN-I2-061-20260828T151739812459Z","requirement_id":"I2-061","event_type":"validator_feedback_possible_reversal","iteration":4,"prior_feedback_history":["Remove the invented mandatory thickness requirement: this clause prohibits direct calculations as an alternative and does not independently require a thickness value or calculation-case existence; retain thickness only as an optional typed/unit-constrained operand if needed. Also encode the prohibition explicitly so directCalculationMethodValue cannot be used as the calculationMethod for an applicable shell-plating or local-frame case, while preserving the prescribedAnalyticalProcedure applicability scope rather than requiring this structure for every calculation case.","Preserve the prior repair, but remove the global sh:minCount 1 constraints on calculationCaseAssessedHullStructure and calculationMethod. The requirement does not require every calculation case to have an assessed structure or method; retain these paths and the optional typed/unit-constrained thickness operand, and make the prohibition conditional only for a case whose assessed hull structure is explicitly plating or structuralMember. The prescribedAnalyticalProcedure alternative must remain valid for applicable cases, while directCalculationMethodValue must fail only in that applicable scope.","Preserve the prior repairs, but add the prescribedAnalyticalProcedure alternative explicitly. The current graph only forbids directCalculationMethodValue for applicable plating or structuralMember cases and never constrains calculationMethod to permit/encode the required prescribed analytical procedure alternative. Keep calculationCaseAssessedHullStructure and calculationMethod optional, retain the conditional prohibition only for explicitly typed plating or structuralMember cases, and keep thickness optional with its existing hullStructure-owned quantity and unit constraints."],"current_feedback":"Preserve the prior repairs: keep calculationCaseAssessedHullStructure, calculationMethod, and thickness optional, and apply the rule only when the assessed structure is explicitly typed nltl:plating or nltl:structuralMember. The current SPARQL has accidental pass/fail logic: NOT EXISTS prescribedAnalyticalProcedure makes a case with no method fail, despite no existence requirement. Instead, reject directCalculationMethodValue in the applicable scope, and constrain any present calculationMethod to the prescribedAnalyticalProcedure alternative without requiring that property. Ensure unrelated or multiple method values cannot bypass that alternative; retain the hullStructure-owned optional thickness quantity and metre unit constraints.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
